concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-16j a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16J Delegation by Commission"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-16j ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate all or any of its functions or powers under this Act to a Commissioner. Note: Sections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain provisions relating to delegations.  (2) In exercising a delegated function or power, the delegate must comply with any written directions of the Commission.  (3) The delegation continues in force despite a change in the constitution of the Commission.  (4) The delegation may be varied or revoked by resolution of the Commission (whether or not there has been a change in the constitution of the Commission).  (5) A certificate signed by the Chair stating any matter with respect to the delegation is prima facie evidence of the matter.  (6) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in subsection (5) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been duly given unless the contrary is established.  Amendments  Schedule 1" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commission may, by resolution, delegate all or any of its functions or powers under this Act to a Commissioner. Note: Sections 34AA to 34A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 contain provisions relating to delegations.  (2) In exercising a delegated function or power, the delegate must comply with any written directions of the Commission.  (3) The delegation continues in force despite a change in the constitution of the Commission.  (4) The delegation may be varied or revoked by resolution of the Commission (whether or not there has been a change in the constitution of the Commission).  (5) A certificate signed by the Chair stating any matter with respect to the delegation is prima facie evidence of the matter.  (6) A document purporting to be a certificate mentioned in subsection (5) is taken to be such a certificate and to have been duly given unless the contrary is established.  Amendments  Schedule 1"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a8943ff655c33bc193956d5215da559b28b893b00759888dbf3ebccce907384a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-16j-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-16j-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-16j-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-16j-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-16j-ss-5 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-centre-for-international-agricultural-research-amendment-act-2007-sch-1-sec-16j-ss-6 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
