doc:sch-2-sec-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4 Certificates relating to vesting of land" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This item applies if:  (a) any land vests in the Commonwealth under this Part; and  (b) there is lodged with a land registration official a certificate that:  (i) is signed by the Minister; and  (ii) identifies the land, whether by reference to a map or otherwise; and  (iii) states that the land has become vested in the Commonwealth under this Part. Note: Certificates under paragraph (1)(b) are presumed to be authentic: see item 17. (2) The land registration official may:  (a) register the matter in a way that is the same as, or similar to, the way in which dealings in land of that kind are registered; and  (b) deal with, and give effect to, the certificate.  Transitional provisions  Schedule 2 Assets, liabilities and legal proceedings  Part 2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

